# Environment files.

# `.env` is untracked: it holds local values, and the point is that no NEW secret added

# there ever reaches the repository. `.env.example` stays tracked — it is the template.

.env

.env.local

.env.*.local

!.env.example

#

# NOT listed, deliberately: `.env.production`. The deploy workflow has no `env:` block, so

# the production build reads the Supabase URL and publishable key from that file IN the

# repository. Untracking it before moving those values into Actions secrets, and referencing

# them from the workflow, would ship a build with a null Supabase client — and supabase.ts

# fails soft, so votes would stop being recorded with nothing visibly broken.

